    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", "@id": "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#shaheer-ali-khan", name: "Shaheer Ali Khan", honorificSuffix: "PhD", jobTitle: "Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist", url: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/editorial-standards/#who", sameAs: ["https://www.linkedin.com/in/shaheer-ali-khan-data/"], worksFor: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" } },
      datePublished: "2026-11-05",
      dateModified: "2026-11-05",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" },
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      ...(product.brand ? { brand: { "@type": "Brand", name: product.brand } } : {}),
      ...(product.image ? { image: product.image.url } : {}),
      ...(product.priceBounds
        ? {
            offers: {
              "@type": "AggregateOffer",
              priceCurrency: "USD",
              lowPrice: product.priceBounds.low,
              highPrice: product.priceBounds.high,
              url: product.amazonUrl,
            },
          }
        : {}),
    })),
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: 5,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: `https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/lifesmart-treadmills/#${product.id}`,
      })),
    },
  ],
};

// "More in" links: the other pages in this article's hub group.
const HERE = "/lifesmart-treadmills/";
const HUB = SECTIONS.find((s) => s.slug === "brands");
const GROUP = HUB?.groups.find((g) => g.pages.some((p) => p.url === HERE)) ?? HUB?.groups[0];
const MORE = (GROUP?.pages ?? []).filter((p) => p.url !== HERE).slice(0, 6);
---

<Layout
  title={`${title} | Treadmill Reviews USA`}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: "2026-11-05",
    modifiedTime: "2026-11-05",
    author: "Shaheer Ali Khan",
    section: "Fitness Equipment",
    tags: [
      "lifesmart treadmill",
      "lifesmart tm4500 powertouch treadmill",
      "lifesmart tm6500 powertouch treadmill",
      "lifesmart tm4800 treadmill",
      "lifesmart tm3000 powertouch treadmill",
      "lifesmart tm4000c treadmill",
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
  stickyCta={{ text: "Best LifeSmart: LifeSmart TM4000C", link: PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl }}
>
  <article class="ed-article" data-template="editorial">
    <div class="ed-col">
      <nav class="ed-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/brands/">Brands</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        <span>Buyer’s Guide</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="ed-title">LifeSmart Treadmills: The PowerTouch Range Explained</h1>
      <p class="ed-dek">
        LifeSmart treadmills are the self-folding PowerTouch machines you see at Costco and Dick’s Sporting Goods. The best-known of them, the TM4500, has been discontinued, and the range now runs from the TM3000 to the touchscreen TM6500, with Costco-only models alongside. This guide sets out what is current, what each model costs, which published figures disagree, and the one thing every buyer should know first: a one-year warranty.
      </p>

      <!-- Byline -->
      <div class="ed-byline">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="44" height="44" />
        <div class="ed-byline-text">
          By <a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a><br />
          Updated November 5, 2026 · Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS
        </div>
        <a href="#top-picks" class="btn-ghost">View products</a>
      </div>
      <p class="ed-disclosure">
        We research every product on this page independently. If you buy through our links, we may earn a
        commission at no cost to you. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Learn more about how we review.</a>
      </p>

      <div class="ed-body prose prose-lg">
        <p class="ed-lead">
          LifeSmart's pitch is one feature: PowerTouch, a motorised fold that raises and lowers the deck at the press
          of a button, with infrared sensors meant to stop it lowering onto a pet or a child. Around that it builds
          brushless-motor folding treadmills with incline and a small decline, sold mainly through Costco and Dick's
          Sporting Goods and on its own store. The names are confusing — TM3000, TM3000C, TM4000, TM4000C, TM4500,
          TM4800, TM5000, TM6500, TM55, TM22X — and so are some of the figures. This guide sorts out which models are
          current, which are retailer-specific, what each one costs, and how a LifeSmart compares with similarly priced
          treadmills that carry much longer warranties.
        </p>

        <section id="top-picks" class="ed-toppicks not-prose">
          <h2>Our top picks:</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Best LifeSmart:</span> <a href="#lifesmart-tm4000c">LifeSmart TM4000C</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[0].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Budget Pick:</span> <a href="#lifesmart-tm3000">LifeSmart TM3000</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[1].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Most Incline:</span> <a href="#lifesmart-tm5000">LifeSmart TM5000</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[2].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Costco Only:</span> <a href="#lifesmart-tm6500">LifeSmart TM6500</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[3].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="tp-label"><span class="tp-award">Discontinued:</span> <a href="#lifesmart-tm4500">LifeSmart TM4500</a></span>
              <a href={PRODUCTS[4].amazonUrl} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" class="buy-pill">Amazon &rarr;</a>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <aside class="ed-note not-prose">
          <span class="ed-note-k">What we checked</span>
          <strong class="text-gray-900">What we checked, and what we have not done.</strong> On
          5 November 2026 we checked LifeSmart's US treadmill store (its full product catalogue with prices and stock
          flags, the TM3000, TM4000, TM4000C, TM4500 and TM5000 product pages, its warranty page and its About page),
          Costco's product pages for the TM6500 and TM55 (Costco's pages did not show prices to our requests, and its
          TM4500 page refused them), Action Lifestyle's TM4000C listing and a Costco deal tracker's TM4800 entry in
          search results, an open-box retailer's TM4800 listing, a fitness retailer's LifeSmart brand guide and Sole's
          blog coverage of the TM4500, and the US Consumer Product Safety Commission's recall database for LifeSmart.
          Several LifeSmart figures differ between LifeSmart, Costco and retailers; conflicts are set out in the text
          and kept off the cards, and where only LifeSmart publishes a figure we say so. Prices are those shown on the
          day and change often. We have not tested any LifeSmart treadmill. As an Amazon Associate we earn from
          qualifying purchases; that does not change what we say.
        </aside>

        <nav class="ed-toc not-prose" aria-label="In this guide">
          <h2>In this guide</h2>
          <ol>
            <li><a href="#short-answer">Should You Buy a LifeSmart Treadmill? The Short Answer</a></li>
            <li><a href="#who-is-lifesmart">Who Makes LifeSmart Treadmills?</a></li>
            <li><a href="#lineup">The Range</a></li>
            <li><a href="#tm4500">The TM4500</a></li>
            <li><a href="#costco-models">Costco Models</a></li>
            <li><a href="#warranty">The Warranty</a></li>
            <li><a href="#motors-decline">Motors and Decline</a></li>
            <li><a href="#alternatives">LifeSmart vs Similar Treadmills</a></li>
            <li><a href="#faq">Frequently asked questions</a></li>
          </ol>
        </nav>

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Should You Buy a LifeSmart Treadmill? The Short Answer</h2>
<p>
            <strong>Only if the automatic PowerTouch fold matters to you. LifeSmart treadmills are reasonably specified
            for the price, but every LifeSmart carries a one-year limited warranty on functional parts, and the
            best-known model, the TM4500, is discontinued. If you do buy one, the TM4000C at $1,199 is the pick.</strong>
          </p>
          <p>
            On 5 November 2026 LifeSmart's own store listed the TM3000 at $999, the TM4000C at $1,199 and the TM5000 at
            $1,699, with cheaper TM2000-series machines below them, and marked the TM4500 as discontinued with the
            TM4000C as its replacement. Costco sells its own LifeSmart models, the touchscreen TM6500 and the budget TM55
            among them, and the TM4800 has appeared in Costco warehouses. Figures for some models differ between
            LifeSmart, Costco and retailers.
          </p>
          <p>
            The warranty is the deciding issue. LifeSmart's warranty page says it offers "a 1 year limited warranty on all
            products", covering functional parts for personal use, with claims made through the retailer. For similar
            money, the <a href="/bowflex-t6-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Bowflex T6</a> and the <a href="/horizon-7-0-at-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Horizon 7.0 AT</a> come with
            far longer frame and motor cover. We have not tested any LifeSmart treadmill.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="who-is-lifesmart" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Who Makes LifeSmart Treadmills?</h2>
<p>
            LifeSmart is a consumer-products brand rather than a fitness specialist. Its treadmill store's About page
            calls it "a trusted legacy brand" and lists its other products: space heaters sold at Walmart, Home Depot and
            Lowe's, and <a href="/best-zero-gravity-massage-chairs/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>massage chairs</a> at BJ's and Menards. The same page and its support contacts point to Supply Chain
            Sources (SCS), which a retailer's brand guide places in Allen, Texas, and describes as LifeSmart's partner for
            fitness equipment and warranty support. LifeSmart's fitness support email is on an SCS domain.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Not LifeSpan, and not the Chinese LifeSmart</h3>
          <p>
            LifeSmart is easily confused with two other names. <a href="/lifespan-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">LifeSpan Fitness</a> is a separate Utah treadmill maker best known for walking and desk treadmills. And a Chinese smart-home
            company also called LifeSmart is unrelated. Everything on this page refers to the US treadmill brand sold at
            Costco and Dick's.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">What PowerTouch is</h3>
          <p>
            PowerTouch is LifeSmart's motorised folding system: press a button and the deck raises to its storage
            position or lowers to use, without lifting. LifeSmart says proprietary sensors detect objects under or near
            the treadmill and stop the deck lowering if the area is not clear. Most <a href="/folding-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>folding treadmills</a> use a gas strut
            that assists you lifting the deck; PowerTouch removes the lift entirely, which matters to buyers with back
            problems or limited strength. We have not verified how the sensors perform, so keep children and pets clear
            regardless.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="lineup" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>The LifeSmart Treadmill Range in November 2026</h2>
<p>
            LifeSmart sells different models in different places, which is the main source of confusion. The table
            groups them by where we found them on 5 November 2026.
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[620px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
